- When `x` is even, `k1` and `k2` are mathematically equal (`x // 2 == (x + 1) // 2`). The code redundantly executes a full $O(\log M)$ bit-lifting traversal to calculate `sum2`, which can just be set to `sum1`.
- The dictionary `val_to_idx` is unnecessarily queried inside the sliding window loop for every element addition and removal. Precomputing an array of mapped indices (e.g., `mapped_nums = [val_to_idx[v] for v in nums]`) avoids these repetitive dict lookups and speeds up execution significantly.
